  "title": "Rabban Bar Sauma's embassy to Europe",
  "summary": "In 1287 the Nestorian monk Rabban Bar Sauma left Baghdad as envoy of the Il-khan Arghun to seek a Christian alliance. He travelled through Armenia and Constantinople to Rome, then Paris and Bordeaux, meeting Philip IV and Edward I, and in 1288 received communion from Pope Nicholas IV. No military help followed, but he left an account of the journey.",
