  "reviewer_note": "Least sure: stop order and dates. Only Baghdad (1287) and the 1288 papal meeting carry years; the rest follow the order of the Gale narrative and are undated. Rome appears twice (arrival before the pope was elected, then 1288). The second Gale entry mentions Naples and Genoa stops, which are not used. Gale entries conflict on when he wrote his account, so only its existence is stated. Both Gale pages are one publisher; Iranica is the independent source for the 1287 embassy and 1288 return.",
